# Help popout `?` — use `FLOQRHelpAttach` only

Do **not** hand-place `details.help-popout`, invent flex/CSS positioning, or convert helper paragraphs ad-hoc.

## Required module

File: `help-attach.js`  
API: `window.FLOQRHelpAttach`

Script order on pages that show `?`:

1. `floqai-help-repository.js` (if FloqAi search is used)
2. `help-attach.js`
3. `helper-popouts.js` (legacy converters call HelpAttach; do not bypass)

## Attach API (only way to add `?`)

```js
FLOQRHelpAttach.attach({
  target: headingOrLabelEl,   // verbiage host (h2, label, span…)
  title: "Display Security Setting",
  body: "Plain-text help…",          // or bodyHtml: "<p>…</p>"
  searchPhrases: ["display security", "ip allowlist"],
  links: [{ label: "Security Logs", href: "…" }],
  id: "help-display-security"
});
```

Effects (guaranteed by the module):

- Wraps verbiage in `.help-label` > `.help-label-text`
- Appends `?` as a sibling **immediately beside** the text (`width: fit-content`, no far-right drift)
- Registers copy into `FLOQRHelpRepository` when present

Declarative alternative:

```html
<h2 data-floqr-help-title="…" data-floqr-help-body="…" data-floqr-help-search="phrase|phrase">Title</h2>
```

(`FLOQRHelpAttach.mountAll()` runs on DOMContentLoaded.)

## Forbidden

- Lone `details.help-popout` not created via `FLOQRHelpAttach`
- Stretching `.help-label` with `flex: 1` / `width: 100%` (pushes `?` to the far edge)
- Orphan `?` replacing `p.sub.small` without attaching beside the heading
- One-off CSS “fixes” for `?` position — fix/extend `help-attach.js` instead

## Checklist

- [ ] Called `FLOQRHelpAttach.attach` (or `data-floqr-help-*` + mountAll)
- [ ] `help-attach.js` loaded before any help conversion
- [ ] Verbiage mirrored in `floqai-help-repository.js` when it is a new patron/admin help topic
- [ ] Previewed: `?` sits beside the label on PC / tablet / phone
